Box86 patch 24 -- publish the Wine 11 Wayland callback slots atomically.

Apply after patch 23.

Wine's process Wayland connection has a blocking event-dispatch loop, while
clipboard and surface objects can install listeners from other call paths.
Patch 23 serialized allocation of the fixed listener slots, but its native ARM
callback stubs still read ordinary global pointers.  Do not make correctness
depend on undocumented ordering across the subsequent libwayland call.

Use a C11 release store when a guest callback table is assigned to one of the
six listener classes covered or corrected by patch 23, and an acquire load in
each matching native callback.  Relaxed loads are sufficient for lookup while
the patch-23 registry mutex excludes other writers.  Callback dispatch remains
lock-free; no render/audio logging or performance claim is added.

